{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_openapi_paths_pr_cs_send_to_qcf__rfq_number___vendor_batch__sendtoqcf", "label": "sendToQCF - POST /pr/cs/send-to-qcf/{rfq_number}/{vendor_batch}", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/openapi/paths/pr_cs_send_to_qcf_{rfq_number}_{vendor_batch}.yaml", "source_location": "L2:post", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The happy-path terminus of the CS stage: creates a Quotation Comparison Form from approved RFQ items, emails the CL for final approval, after which items proceed to SAP Auto PO synchronization. Unlike its sibling dispatch actions it declares a real typed schema with required items and rfq_tipe rather than an empty object."}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_openapi_paths_pr_cs_send_to_qcf__rfq_number___vendor_batch__sendtoqcfrequest", "label": "SendToQCF Request Body (items[] + rfq_tipe)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/openapi/paths/pr_cs_send_to_qcf_{rfq_number}_{vendor_batch}.yaml", "source_location": "requestBody.content.application/json.schema", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only fully typed request body among the CS dispatch actions: an object requiring items (array of {id: integer}) and rfq_tipe (string). Its shape is echoed as untyped examples by sendSurrogate, sendRevisiOE and sendIsourcing, so it is the de facto contract for the whole rfq_tipe dispatch family and the candidate for extraction into components/schemas."}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_openapi_paths_pr_cs_send_to_qcf__rfq_number___vendor_batch__sendtoqcf", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_openapi_paths_pr_cl_approve_qcf__qcf_number__clapproveqcf", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/openapi/paths/pr_cs_send_to_qcf_{rfq_number}_{vendor_batch}.yaml", "source_location": "description: 'After